# OpenRouter Free-Only (Hard Rule)

Never route OpenRouter requests to paid/non-free models unless the user explicitly overrides for that exact run.

## Required env defaults

```text
OPENROUTER_FREE_ONLY=true
OPENROUTER_ALLOW_PAID=false
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/owl-alpha
OPENROUTER_EMBEDDING_MODEL=nvidia/llama-nemotron-embed-vl-1b-v2:free
OPENROUTER_RERANK_MODEL=nvidia/llama-nemotron-rerank-vl-1b-v2:free
LEGAL_EMBEDDING_DIM=2048
```

Canonical defaults live in `src/retrieval/openrouter_free_models.js`.

## Allowed OpenRouter model ids

- Curated free stack: `openrouter/owl-alpha`, `nvidia/llama-nemotron-embed-vl-1b-v2:free`, `nvidia/llama-nemotron-rerank-vl-1b-v2:free`
- `openrouter/free` (auto-router fallback)
- Any model id ending in `:free`

## Forbidden without explicit user override

- `openrouter/auto`
- Paid OpenRouter routes (`openai/text-embedding-3-small`, `cohere/rerank-v3.5`, etc.)
- `OPENROUTER_ALLOW_PAID=true`

## Implementation

- All OpenRouter HTTP calls must pass `assertFreeOpenRouterModel()` before request.
- Chat, embedding, and rerank each use role-specific model env vars (do not reuse chat model for embed/rerank).
- If free-only is on and no valid free model is configured, skip OpenRouter and use deterministic/local fallback.
- Paid embeddings/rerank may use non-OpenRouter providers only (OpenAI/Voyage/Cohere direct keys), not OpenRouter.

## Validation

```bash
node ~/.codex/bin/validate-openrouter-free-only.js
```
